  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "$$\n\n$\\int (\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x)\\text{d}x=$",
  "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cosine function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcosh}\u2061x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}+\\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x)\\text{d}x & =4\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\operatorname{sinh}\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{arcosh}\u2061x+\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
